    "clinical_definition": {
      "value": "Tyrosinemia type II is characterized by corneal dystrophy, painful palmoplantar hyperkeratosis, and variable intellectual disability. Individuals diagnosed and treated from early infancy may be asymptomatic or have only mild ocular and skin manifestations. Individuals with delayed diagnosis or lack of treatment present with ocular, skin, and variable cognitive manifestations.",
